[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695133802","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103505#issuecomment-2695133802","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103505","id":2695133802,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gpHpq","user":{"login":"matheusmdx","id":44306054,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MzA2MDU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44306054?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx","html_url":"https://github.com/matheusmdx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matheusmdx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-03T17:49:23Z","updated_at":"2025-03-03T17:49:23Z","body":"This is because you're using `Fit Width Proporcional` in your `TextureRect` nodes. As explained in the `TextureRect.expand_mode` tooltip, this doesn't work well when this node is inside a container and can lead to unstable behavior. This is a known limitation and the only workaround is don't use the cited modes when the parent is a container.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a40868d4-cb2f-433d-9b04-f230e22504d1)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695133802/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695374913","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103505#issuecomment-2695374913","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103505","id":2695374913,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gqChB","user":{"login":"zmn-hamid","id":129656474,"node_id":"U_kgDOB7pmmg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/129656474?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid","html_url":"https://github.com/zmn-hamid","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zmn-hamid/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-03T19:41:35Z","updated_at":"2025-03-03T19:42:51Z","body":"> This is because you're using `Fit Width Proporcional` in your `TextureRect` nodes. As explained in the `TextureRect.expand_mode` tooltip, this doesn't work well when this node is inside a container and can lead to unstable behavior. This is a known limitation and the only workaround is don't use the cited modes when the parent is a container.\n> \n> ![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a40868d4-cb2f-433d-9b04-f230e22504d1)\n\nOh thanks for the help, got it. But how am I supposed to resize down a texture then? I wanna add a semi high res asset and put it in smaller sizes over the app, and the only way I could come up with was using expand and stretch modes so at least I can roughly resize it to whatever size I want. Otherwise the asset doesn't go lower than the base size. sorry if I shouldn't have asked a different question here","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2695374913/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]